        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Own The Join",
          "text": "If two subgraphs bounce a query back and forth, the domain boundary is wrong. Move the join into one service instead of tuning the hops."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Failure Modes And Anti-Patterns (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "# reviews",
            "type Review { body: String!",
            "  author: User  product: Product }",
            "type User @key(fields: \"id\") {",
            "  id: ID! @external",
            "  reviews: [Review] }"
          ],
          "note": "this is the cross-service join"
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "The Products Subgraph SDL",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "# products",
            "type Product @key(fields: \"upc\") {",
            "  upc: String!  name: String!",
            "  price: Int! }",
            "type Query {",
            "  topProducts: [Product] }"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Three Subgraphs And Ownership",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Subgraphs",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "# accounts",
            "type User @key(fields: \"id\") {",
            "  id: ID!  name: String! }",
            "type Query { me: User }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "accounts owns `User.name` and the `me` root field",
            "products owns `Product` and `topProducts`",
            "reviews re-declares both types by ==key== alone",
            "Borrowed key fields carry `@external`, nothing more"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Who Owns What"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Subgraph",
            "Key",
            "Owns"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "accounts",
              "`id`",
              "name, me"
            ],
            [
              "products",
              "`upc`",
              "name, price"
            ],
            [
              "reviews",
              "both",
              "body, reviews"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Reading The SDL",
          "items": [
            "`@key` = how others find this type",
            "`@external` = owned somewhere else",
            "No `@key` = plain value type"
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Re-declare, Don't Copy",
          "text": "`reviews` never stores a user's name. It declares `User` by key and adds **one** field — the gateway fills in the rest."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "A Worked Supergraph",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "One Client Query"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "{ me { name reviews {",
            "  body product { name price } } } }",
            "# spans all three subgraphs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Plan It Builds"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "accounts: me",
              "Flatten(me)",
              "reviews: _entities",
              "Flatten(product)",
              "products: _entities"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Three round trips, and only three",
            "Every review's product resolves in one batched `_entities`",
            "Add `Review.product @provides(fields: \"name\")` and hop three vanishes",
            "That holds only while clients ask for `name` alone"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Migrating A Field"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "# new pricing subgraph",
            "price: Int! @override(from: \"products\")",
            "# ship, verify traffic, then delete old field"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`rover dev` runs router plus subgraphs locally",
            "It recomposes the supergraph on every file change",
            "Same composition errors you would hit in CI"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Take These Away"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Entities are the nouns; `@key` is their identity",
            "Reference resolvers are the join implementation",
            "The query plan is the actual execution engine",
            "You buy autonomy and correctness; you pay in round trips"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Final Test",
          "text": "Model subgraphs on domain boundaries you would defend in a design review — never on the service topology you happen to have today."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Subgraphs Stand Alone",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. A Subgraph Is A Server"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Each subgraph is a ==complete GraphQL server== on its own port",
            "It boots, serves and answers without any router present",
            "Start `products` alone and hit it at `localhost:4002`",
            "If it only works behind the gateway, it is **wrong**"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "# products/schema.graphql",
            "type Product @key(fields: \"id\") {",
            "  id: ID!  name: String! }",
            "type Query { topProducts: [Product] }"
          ],
          "note": "runs standalone on port 4002"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Query It Directly In Dev"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Open its own sandbox and run real queries against it",
            "Federation adds `_service` and `_entities` to every subgraph",
            "So you can test the ==join entry point== by hand",
            "No router, no supergraph, no composition step needed"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "# straight at the subgraph",
            "{ _entities(representations: [",
            "  { __typename: \"Product\",",
            "    id: \"1\" }]) { ... on Product",
            "  { name } } }"
          ],
          "note": "exactly what the router sends"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. The Two Extra Root Fields"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Name",
            "What it is"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`_service { sdl }`",
              "raw SDL, directives kept"
            ],
            [
              "`_entities(reps)`",
              "`[_Entity]!` fetched by key"
            ],
            [
              "`_Entity`",
              "union of all `@key` types"
            ],
            [
              "`_Any`",
              "JSON blob + `__typename`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Composition reads `_service`; the router calls `_entities`",
            "`_Entity` unions every type in this subgraph with a `@key`",
            "A representation is just `__typename` plus the key fields",
            "Both root fields stay ==out of== your public schema docs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Never Hand-Write These",
          "text": "`@apollo/subgraph`, gqlgen, strawberry and graphql-java all generate them. Writing them yourself means you drifted from the spec."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Argument one is the ==representation==: `__typename` plus the key",
            "Argument two is context, holding your `dataSources`",
            "Return the entity, or `null` when nothing matches",
            "Batch `byId` behind {blue:DataLoader} or you rebuild N+1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "subtitle": "Run and test in isolation"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Reference Resolvers And Testing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Local Dev Loop",
          "items": [
            "`npm run dev` inside one subgraph folder",
            "`{ _service { sdl } }` prints its own schema",
            "`rover subgraph check` before you publish"
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Reference Resolver Shape"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "Product: {",
            "  __resolveReference: (",
            "    { id }, { dataSources }) =>",
            "    dataSources.products.byId(id)",
            "}"
          ],
          "note": "one key in, one entity out"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Rules You Must Not Break"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Returning results out of input order corrupts every row",
            "Looping the array one key at a time is the N+1",
            "Throwing on a dangling key — return `null` instead",
            "Skipping authorization because the router already checked"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// batch, do not loop",
            "__resolveReference: ({id}, ctx) =>",
            "  ctx.loaders.product.load(id)"
          ],
          "note": "one loader per request"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Independently Runnable",
          "text": "A subgraph you cannot boot, query and test on its own is not a service — it is a fragment of the gateway wearing a port number."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. What To Test Where"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Level",
            "Target"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "unit",
              "field resolvers"
            ],
            [
              "isolation",
              "`_entities` by key"
            ],
            [
              "contract",
              "published SDL"
            ],
            [
              "integration",
              "router + subgraphs"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "# contract test input",
            "representations: [",
            "  { __typename:\"User\", id:\"1\" },",
            "  { __typename:\"User\", id:\"2\" }]"
          ],
          "note": "results must match input order"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Before You Publish",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Subgraph boots with no router running",
            "`_service { sdl }` returns the schema you expect",
            "`_entities` resolves every declared `@key`",
            "Composition check passes against the current graph"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "When It Is Not Called",
          "items": [
            "Query asks only for key fields",
            "Router already has the fields it needs",
            "Partial returns are fine — others resolve on"
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        }
      ],
      "subtitle": "Run and test in isolation"
    }
